  "correct": "E",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Name the repeated power",
      "body": "<p>Put <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>, so the equation becomes quadratic in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "An exponential and its square can be replaced by one positive variable.",
      "pitfall": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></msup><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>, not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.",
      "pause": "Write and factor the quadratic in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow></math>.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b3-l04",
          "reminder": "An exponential and its square can be replaced by one positive variable."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Undo the substitution before adding",
      "body": "Solve your quadratic and check each root is in the exponential’s range. Recover the original roots with logarithms, then combine their sum.",
      "recap": "A sum of logarithms with one base is the logarithm of the product of their positive arguments.",
      "pitfall": "Values of the exponential variable are not the original roots.",
      "pause": "Find the original roots, combine their logarithms and convert the base if necessary.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l06",
          "reminder": "A sum of logarithms with one base is the logarithm of the product of their positive arguments."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p>Set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>. The equation becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>, so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>Thus the two roots in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>3</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>. Their sum is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>15</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>15</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>Answer E.</strong> Both roots are allowed because 3 and 5 lie in the positive range of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></msup></mrow></math>.</p>",
